{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1975","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. 378QAQ and Mocha's Array"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Mocha likes arrays, so before her departure, 378QAQ gave her an array $$$a$$$ consisting of $$$n$$$ positive integers as a gift."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Mocha thinks that $$$a$$$ is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"beautiful"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if there exist two numbers $$$i$$$ and $$$j$$$ ($$$1\\leq i,j\\leq n$$$, $$$i\\neq j$$$) such that for all $$$k$$$ ($$$1 \\leq k \\leq n$$$), $$$a_k$$$ is divisible$$$^\\dagger$$$ by either $$$a_i$$$ or $$$a_j$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Determine whether $$$a$$$ is beautiful."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^\\dagger$$$ $$$x$$$ is divisible by $$$y$$$ if there exists an integer $$$z$$$ such that $$$x = y \\cdot z$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1\\leq t\\leq 500$$$). The description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$3\\leq n\\leq 10^5$$$) — the length of the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_n$$$ ($$$1\\leq a_i \\leq 10^9$$$) — the elements of the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if array $$$a$$$ is beautiful, and output \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"No"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" otherwise."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can output \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"No"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" in any case (for example, strings \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yEs"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" will be recognized as a positive response)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n3\n7 3 8\n5\n7 1 9 3 5\n5\n4 12 2 6 3\n5\n7 49 9 3 1000000000\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nNo\nYes\nYes\nNo\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, any two numbers in the array are coprime, so the answer is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"No"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, we can pick $$$i=2$$$ and $$$j=1$$$. Since every number in the array is divisible by $$$a_i = 1$$$, the answer is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, we can pick $$$i=3$$$ and $$$j=5$$$. $$$2$$$ and $$$4$$$ is divisible by $$$a_i = 2$$$ while $$$3$$$, $$$6$$$ and $$$12$$$ is divisible by $$$a_j = 3$$$, so the answer is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"1975B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1975/problem/B"}